        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fd92b7f5-e7b9-50fb-827e-f753c42b27db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Television Episodes: Empty Orchestra\n- Television Series: Inside No. 9, EastEnders, Red Cap, New Tricks, Paradox\n- People: Steve Pemberton, Reece Shearsmith, Guillem Morales, Tamzin Outhwaite, Sarah Hadland, Emily Howlett, Javone Prince\n- Roles: Melanie Owen, Detective Inspector Rebecca Flint\n- Organizations: BBC One, BBC 2\n\nFacts:\n- Tamzin Outhwaite played Melanie Owen in the BBC One soap opera EastEnders from 1998 until 2002.\n- In 2009, the British science fiction police drama Paradox starred Tamzin Outhwaite as Detective Inspector Rebecca Flint.\n- After gaining national notice in EastEnders, Tamzin Outhwaite starred in theatre and television productions including Red Cap and New Tricks.\n- Empty Orchestra is the fourth episode of the third series of the British dark comedy anthology television programme Inside No. 9.\n- Steve Pemberton and Reece Shearsmith wrote Empty Orchestra, and Guillem Morales directed it.\n- Empty Orchestra first aired on 7 March 2017 on BBC 2.\n- Empty Orchestra is set in a karaoke booth and follows work colleagues Greg, Fran, Connie, Janet, and Duane as they celebrate Roger's promotion.\n- In Empty Orchestra, Reece Shearsmith plays Greg, Sarah Hadland plays Fran, Tamzin Outhwaite plays Connie, Emily Howlett plays Janet, Javone Prince plays Duane, and Steve Pemberton plays Roger.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
